{"id":"627555200","kind":"article","title":"概念图","author":"Piotr Wozniak","original_authors":["Piotr Wozniak"],"original_source_urls":["https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Concept_map"],"publisher":"Jarrett Ye","column":"认知基石 & 教育培训","date":"2023-05-07","updated":"2023-05-07","votes":6,"comment_count":0,"minutes":2,"chars":730,"keywords":["概念图","语义网络","概念化","知识表征","神经网络"],"summary":"该词条把概念图定义为表示知识结构中语义关系的图示，并将其类比为思维中可共同激活的神经概念及其连接。作者认为，概念化中的泛化会筛选并简化这些关系，最终可能形成高度凝练的概念表征；他说明自己在 SuperMemo Guru 中使用“概念图”一词的范围。","zhihu_url":"https://zhuanlan.zhihu.com/p/627555200","restoration":null,"toc":[],"html":"<p data-pid=\"cfa1t8i8\"><b>概念图（Concept map）</b>是源自计算机科学的术语。它可用于表示知识结构中的语义关系（例如在<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Incremental_reading\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">渐进阅读</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-1\"><a href=\"#ref-1\">[1]</a></sup>或<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Neural_creativity\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">神经创造力</a>中）。为了可视化思考过程，概念图可能与<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Grandmother_cell\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">概念细胞</a>及其概念之间的联系（神经元之间的链接）相对应。</p><p data-pid=\"CCrsE2VQ\">在<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Conceptualization\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">概念化</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-2\"><a href=\"#ref-2\">[2]</a></sup>的过程中，<b>概念图</b>经历了<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Generalization\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">泛化</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-2\"><a href=\"#ref-2\">[2]</a></sup>，这倾向于简化它们的结构。泛化是基于在不同上下文中对映射子组件交集的选择性激活。不太相关的<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Concept\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">概念</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-3\"><a href=\"#ref-3\">[3]</a></sup>属性会被<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Forgetting\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">遗忘</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-4\"><a href=\"#ref-4\">[4]</a></sup>。这种不完全结晶的概念在文献中被称为<b>细胞组装体</b>。泛化过程的最终产物可能是<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Grandmother_cell\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">祖母细胞</a>的涌现（见：<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/The_truth_about_grandmother_cells\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">祖母细胞的真相</a>）。有关基于<b>概念图</b>的思维过程模型，请参阅：<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/How_to_solve_any_problem?\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">如何解决任何问题？</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-5\"><a href=\"#ref-5\">[5]</a></sup></p><p data-pid=\"zd-Mm_o4\">在 <a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/SuperMemo_Guru\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">SuperMemo Guru</a> 中，我通常在可以使用「神经网络」的上下文中使用「概念图」这一术语。我这样选择，是为了推广把大脑看作是在思考过程中可激活的<b>概念图网络</b>的观念。当使用「神经网络」一词时，在联结主义模型不适用的情境下，它为联结主义模型留出了空间。</p><p data-pid=\"bKwZjxJv\">当谈到大脑的<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Concept_network\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">概念网络</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-6\"><a href=\"#ref-6\">[6]</a></sup>中有意义的子网络时，使用<b>概念图</b>这个术语也很方便，尤其是当其概念倾向于在思维中同时激活。例如，在某个特定果园采摘苹果的行为可能会激活一个特定的概念图，该概念图可能会逐渐整合到更简单的概念结构中。在整合过程的最后，可能会形成一个单一的<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Grandmother_cell\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">祖母细胞</a>，负责在头脑中表示一个极为有用的想法。</p><hr/><blockquote data-pid=\"MiljyODE\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"http://paratranz.cn/projects/3131\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Thoughts Memo</a> 汉化组译制<br/>感谢主要译者 24h便利店、校对 JarrettYe<br/>原文：<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Concept_map\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Concept map - supermemo.guru</a><br/>本<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Glossary\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">术语表</a>条目用于解释 <a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/SuperMemo_Guru\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">SuperMemo Guru</a> 系列中关于记忆、学习、创造力和解决问题的文本。</blockquote><hr/><ol class=\"references\"><li id=\"ref-1\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-1\">↩</a> 渐进阅读 <a href=\"https://www.yuque.com/supermemo/wiki/incremental_reading\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.yuque.com/supermemo/wiki/incremental_reading</a></li><li id=\"ref-2\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-2\">↩</a> 泛化与概念化 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"264989664\" href=\"#/post/264989664\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-3\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-3\">↩</a> 概念 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"571218385\" href=\"#/post/571218385\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-4\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-4\">↩</a> 遗忘 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"558542113\" href=\"#/post/558542113\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-5\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-5\">↩</a> 如何解决任何问题？ <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"351779186\" href=\"#/post/351779186\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-6\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-6\">↩</a> 概念网络 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"266541480\" href=\"#/post/266541480\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li></ol>","rec_chain":[{"id":"622160874","title":"「好奇心」具有负面涵义","author":"Susan Edelman","votes":7,"minutes":1,"reason":"同专栏上一篇 · 认知基石 & 教育培训"},{"id":"627546446","title":"神经学谬误","author":"Piotr Wozniak","votes":29,"minutes":24,"reason":"同专栏下一篇 · 认知基石 & 教育培训"},{"id":"351779186","title":"如何解决任何问题？","author":"Piotr Wozniak","votes":130,"minutes":40,"reason":"本文直接引用"},{"id":"571218385","title":"概念","author":"Piotr Wozniak","votes":10,"minutes":1,"reason":"本文直接引用"},{"id":"266541480","title":"概念网络","author":"Piotr Wozniak","votes":43,"minutes":10,"reason":"本文直接引用"}],"rec_bridge":[{"id":"564164660","title":"杏仁体可能涉及到奖励新奇的输入","author":"Edmund T. Rolls","votes":6,"minutes":1,"reason":"跨学派视角 · Edmund T. Rolls"},{"id":"689271349","title":"喜欢和渴望所涉及的神经回路","author":"Susana Peciña","votes":21,"minutes":1,"reason":"跨学派视角 · Susana Peciña"},{"id":"562035095","title":"感受学习乐趣的过程涉及到阿片受体","author":"Irving Biederman","votes":8,"minutes":1,"reason":"跨学派视角 · Irving Biederman"}],"rec_answers":[{"id":"1938889102624792640","title":"高中生，看了很多中式教育和阶级的视频，没有学习动力怎么办？","author":"Thoughts Memo","votes":170,"minutes":4,"reason":"核心节选引用 · 170 赞同","evidence":"正文引用锚点“概念图”明确定位到该译文的标题或主题词。"},{"id":"122307619354","title":"是什么让你突然有了学习的欲望？","author":"Thoughts Memo","votes":77,"minutes":4,"reason":"核心节选引用 · 77 赞同","evidence":"正文链接锚文本明确指向该译文标题或具体关键词。"}]}